1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,720
Are you the kind of person who hated school?
你是那种讨厌上学的人吗？

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:09,510
Or are you more like Michael Nicholson, who can't stop learning?
还是说，你更像迈克尔·尼科尔森无法停止学习？

3
00:00:09,510 --> 00:00:16,650
He currently has 30 degrees including 22 master's and a doctorate!
他目前拥有30个学位，其中包括22个硕士学位和1个博士学位！

4
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:24,880
If you're also passionate about studying, you might be a philomath – a person who loves to learn and study.
如果你同样热衷于学习，那你可能就是一名“爱学者”——指热爱学习和钻研的人。

5
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:31,940
The word comes from Greek with 'phil' meaning 'a lover of' and 'math' meaning 'learning'.
这个词源于希腊语，“phil”意为“热爱……的人”，“math”则表示“学习”。

6
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:38,870
Humans are all philomaths to an extent – our brain is hardwired to be curious.
从某种程度上来说，人类都是热爱学习的人——我们的大脑天生就具备好奇心。

7
00:00:38,870 --> 00:00:46,300
We want to learn and understand, partly to make sense of the world but also because of something called neoteny.
我们渴望学习和理解事物，一部分是为了认清世界的运行规律，另一部分则是源于一种名为“幼态延续”的现象。

8
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:56,320
This is a term that refers to the juvenile characteristics of some animals, including humans, being retained into adulthood.
这个术语指的是部分动物（包括人类）在成年后依然保留着幼年时期的特征。

9
00:00:56,320 --> 00:01:07,130
One of these traits is neuroplasticity, which helps our brains stay flexible – this gives us the ability to learn throughout our lives.
其中一项特征就是神经可塑性，它能让我们的大脑保持灵活，让我们拥有终身学习的能力。

10
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:15,730
Many creatures which are genetically close to us, like primates, can't do this and only learn during their adolescence.
许多和我们基因相近的生物，比如灵长类动物，就不具备这种能力，它们的学习能力只存在于青春期。

11
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:22,590
But for every person who loves learning, there are plenty who can't stand it.
不过，有多少人热爱学习，就有多少人对学习深恶痛绝。

12
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:28,500
Lots of people remember their school days as being boring or even pointless.
很多人回忆起学生时代，都觉得那段时光枯燥乏味，甚至毫无意义。

13
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,320
Why is this?
这是为什么呢？

14
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:41,320
Educational anthropologists have suggested that if a concept or idea is too complex or dull, it becomes harder to link old and new ideas together.
教育人类学家指出，如果某个概念或知识点过于复杂、乏味，人们就很难将新旧知识串联起来。

15
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:47,140
If that's the case, we lose motivation and absorb less information.
一旦出现这种情况，我们就会失去学习动力，吸收的知识也会大打折扣。

16
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:55,530
This negative experience of education at school may lead to people avoiding learning opportunities in later life.
这种糟糕的校园学习经历，可能会导致人们在成年后刻意回避学习的机会。

17
00:01:55,530 --> 00:02:02,500
So, don't let a bad educational experience prevent you learning something new as an adult.
所以，不要让一段糟糕的求学经历，阻碍你在成年后学习新事物的脚步。

18
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:11,060
Evolution has made us lifelong learners, so take advantage of your biology and discover your inner philomath.
进化让我们成为了终身学习者，所以请好好利用自身的生理优势，发掘内心深处那个热爱学习的自己吧。

19
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:13,420
Who knows what you could achieve?
谁知道你能取得怎样的成就呢？
